## 3. Understanding Data Leakage

One of the most important concepts I learned in this exercise was **data leakage**.

Data leakage occurs when information that would not actually be available at the time of prediction is used as a model feature.

I learned to apply the **day-before test**:

> Would this value exist, with this value, the day before the subscriber churned?

If the answer is no, that column should not be used for predicting churn.

This helped me understand that a very high model score can sometimes be misleading if the model has access to information that reveals the outcome.

